            <ArticleTitle>Blue Rubber Bleb Nevus Syndrome: Promising Response To Sirolimus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>53-54</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Blue rubber bleb nevus syndrome is a rare disease involving venous malformations.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE CHARACTERISTICS" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED">We present a 6-year-old female with the syndrome, and consumptive coagulopathy.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="INTERVENTION/OUTCOME" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED">After management with sirolimus, symptoms resolved.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MESSAGE" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED">Sirolimus may be a valuable option for reducing bleeding complications and cosmetic sequelae for the patients with this syndrome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
